# CMMI Audit Platform — Upload Practice Area Folder connector configuration
#
# Copy this file to .env.local (Vite loads .env.local automatically and it
# is gitignored by default) and fill in the values you have.
#
# Vite exposes every VITE_-prefixed variable to the client bundle. All of
# the values below are OAuth *client* IDs / public API keys, not secrets —
# the connectors use PKCE / public-client OAuth flows that require no
# client secret. Do not put an actual client secret in any VITE_ variable.

# ── GitHub connector ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No configuration required. Public repositories work with zero setup.
# A Personal Access Token (for private repos or to avoid GitHub's
# unauthenticated rate limit) is entered per-session directly in the
# "Upload Practice Area Folder" UI — it is never read from an env var and
# never persisted.

# ── SharePoint connector (Microsoft Graph + MSAL) ────────────────────────
# Register an Azure AD app (Azure Portal > App registrations > New
# registration > Single-page application), grant it the delegated Graph
# permissions Sites.Read.All and Files.Read.All, and add this app's origin
# as a SPA redirect URI. Then set:
VITE_SHAREPOINT_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_SHAREPOINT_TENANT_ID=

# ── Google Drive connector (Google Identity Services + Picker + Drive API v3) ──
# Create a Google Cloud project, enable the Google Drive API and the Google
# Picker API, create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application) with this
# app's origin as an authorized JavaScript origin, and create an API key
# restricted to the Drive/Picker APIs. Then set:
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# Until the SharePoint / Google Drive variables above are set, those two
# source options in "Upload Practice Area Folder" show a clear "not
# configured" message instead of a broken sign-in button — Local Folder and
# GitHub work regardless.
